module Core

### The protocol for a value that can be STORED at an implicit-copy site.
### `Assignable` gates the `=` operator and every position that implicitly copies a value:
### `var x = a`, passing as a non-`steal` argument, returning a non-`T` value, and `with`
### lens-copy. Auto-derived for any type whose `@llvm` layout contains no `ptr` (and for
### `@llvm("void")`). Types with managed-pointer payloads (`Retained[T]`, `Text`, …) opt in by
### writing `obeys Assignable` and an `assign` body that spells out each field's verb (a refcount
### bump / COW share), centralising the cost in one visible place. `Assignable obeys Copyable`:
### anything you can shallow-`assign` (share) you can also `duplicate`, and its `duplicate` DEFAULTS to
### `assign` (for a managed leaf the share IS the independent copy — same immutable buffer, refcount-held).
### The reverse does NOT hold: an aggregate (List/Dict) is `Copyable` (deep) but NOT `Assignable` (a
### single-owner entity cannot be shallow-shared), so `Assignable` is the STRONGER, narrower capability.
### `needs Assignable everywhere` auto-confers Assignable on any member-bearing type all of whose members
### are themselves Assignable — the structural gate that drives the auto-derived `assign`.
protocol Assignable obeys Copyable
needs Assignable everywhere
  ### Produces the value to bind at the store/assignment destination. For auto-derived types this
  ### is a bitwise duplicate; for opt-in managed types it is the cheap COW share (e.g. a refcount
  ### bump). The heavier deep, independent duplicate is `Copyable.duplicate` (which, for an Assignable
  ### type, defaults to this `assign`).
  ### :returns: The value to store into the destination slot.
  @[readonly, inline]
  routine Me.assign() -> Me
